# Dev environment resources — local notes template

**This is the `.example` template that IS committed.** Copy this to `infra/dev-resources.md` (gitignored) and fill in the real values as Sprint 1.1+ creates each resource.

Per `docs/DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md` "Public-repo hygiene":
- Real Azure resource names, tenant ID, subscription ID, connection strings, deployment tokens **MUST NOT** land in any committed file.
- This template uses `<placeholder>` for every real value. Your filled-in `dev-resources.md` is gitignored.

If you accidentally `git add` `dev-resources.md`, the `.gitignore` entry prevents it, but double-check with `git status` before every commit anyway.

---

